  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multisectoral Response to the communities affected by malnutrition</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide nutrition, water, sanitation and hygiene (WASH), as well as health assistance to vulnerable communities in north-east Nigeria affected by malnutrition. This UNICEF project provides life-saving treatment to children suffering from severe acute malnutrition, screens children for malnutrition, counsels pregnant and lactating women on feeding practices, installs and rehabilitates boreholes to improve water supply, provides WASH facilities and supplies, trains healthcare workers on management of disease outbreaks, and provides life-saving primary healthcare services, among other activities. The project provides humanitarian assistance to 251,001 people in the Nutrition sector, including 126,000 women, 125,001 children, and 27,611 persons with disabilities; 146,859 people in the WASH sector, including 32,954 women, 85,949 children, and 16,155 persons with disabilities; and 300,000 people in the Health sector, including 75,000 women, 185,000 children, and 7,996 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
